      "created_at": "2025-03-16T12:31:02.542Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Ok, nice videos but the logic behind this is still unclear to me. Could I withold end of year bonus so that each month employee works it generates as widtheld Salary Component. Then at the end of year or employee terminates employement I can release that bonus (salary component) but to that moment?</p>\n<p>So basically: lets say employee A starts working on 2nd of Jan 2025. Works still 12th December 2025, I will give them a bonus worth 10% of their monthly wage but payable at end of the month.</p>\n<p>Optionally, if employee leaves 6 months into the job, they can request the full amount of their accrued bonus upto date of relieve?</p>\n<p>Accounting wise this remains as Accounts Payable until encashment date.</p>\n<p>Would this be correct?</p>",
